                    "message": "@prithvi24pai@gmail.com I've verified the updated change on our platform and it meets our requirements. Thanks."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Control/Boot/BootOrder.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Why are these arbitrary strings still?  I've given this same feedback over and over on this feature."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Control/Boot/BootOrder.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Prithvi Pai",
                        "email": "prithvi24pai@gmail.com",
                        "username": "PrithviPai24"
                    },
                    "message": "As per the feedback, added a WIP to throw Invalid Arguments when unacceptable values are SET https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bios-settings-mgr/+/83749\nAs per UEFI Spec, BootOrder values can range from Boot0000-BootFFFF\nhttps://uefi.org/specs/UEFI/2.10/03_Boot_Manager.html\n```\nEach load option entry resides in a Boot####, Driver####, SysPrep####, OsRecovery#### or PlatformRecovery#### variable where #### is replaced by a unique option number in printable hexadecimal representation using the digits 0-9, and the upper case versions of the characters A-F (0000-FFFF)\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Control/Boot/BootOrder.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Prithvi Pai",
                        "email": "prithvi24pai@gmail.com",
                        "username": "PrithviPai24"
                    },
                    "message": "Resolving the comments please let me know if anything needs to be changed"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Control/Boot/BootOrder.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Zoey YJ Chung",
                        "email": "zoey.yj.chung.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "zoeychung10"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi @patrick@stwcx.xyz,\n\nCould you please review this change and merge it if there are no further concerns? Thank you!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Control/Boot/BootOrder.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't think the comment about string usage has been addressed. Why not make these enuma?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Control/Boot/BootOrder.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Prithvi Pai",
                        "email": "prithvi24pai@gmail.com",
                        "username": "PrithviPai24"
                    },
                    "message": "As per UEFI Spec, BootOrder values can range from Boot0000-BootFFFF\nhttps://uefi.org/specs/UEFI/2.10/03_Boot_Manager.html\nSo having enums is not feasible in this case. Have addressed the issue mentioned by Patrick https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bios-settings-mgr/+/83749"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Control/Boot/BootOrder.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Is this expected to be preserved?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Control/Boot/BootOrder.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Prithvi Pai",
                        "email": "prithvi24pai@gmail.com",
                        "username": "PrithviPai24"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, it is expected to be preserved. The values change when host applies the pending values during the upcoming boot"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Control/Boot/BootOrder.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Prithvi Pai",
                        "email": "prithvi24pai@gmail.com",
                        "username": "PrithviPai24"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
